-- title:
--   Residue package for the two legs of the T_q degeneracy roof
-- statement:
--   Fix a natural number $p \neq 0$ and a prime $\ell$ with $\ell \nmid p$, and write $R_\ell$ for the subring of $\mathbf{Q}$ consisting of those rationals whose denominator is coprime to $\ell$. Let $X$ be a scheme with a morphism $c \colon X \to \operatorname{Spec} R_\ell$ that is proper, smooth of relative dimension $1$ and geometrically integral; let $M_0$ be a `CurveModel` over $\mathbf{Q}$ of the field `modularFunctionFieldFull p` (the subfield of $\mathbf{Q}((q))$ generated by the $q$-expansions $j(q^d)$ for $d \mid p$), and $e_0$ an isomorphism from $M_0.C$ to the base change $X \times_{\operatorname{Spec} R_\ell} \operatorname{Spec} \mathbf{Q}$ compatible with the structure maps to $\operatorname{Spec} \mathbf{Q}$; let $q$ be a prime and $M'$ a `CurveModel` over $\mathbf{Q}$ of `modularFunctionFieldFull (p * q)`. Put $X_{\mathbf{Q}}$ for that base change and $c_{\mathbf{Q}}$ for its projection to $\operatorname{Spec} \mathbf{Q}$, and regard the function fields of $X_{\mathbf{Q}}$ and of $M'.C$ as $\mathbf{Q}$-algebras through `baseToFunctionField`. Then, assuming $X_{\mathbf{Q}}$ integral and $c_{\mathbf{Q}}$ smooth of relative dimension $1$, for any two $\mathbf{Q}$-algebra maps $\varphi'_\alpha, \varphi'_\beta \colon \mathbf{Q}(X_{\mathbf{Q}}) \to \mathbf{Q}(M'.C)$ making the target a finite module over the source, the following all hold: both fields are curves over $\mathbf{Q}$ in the sense of `IsCurveOver` (principal divisors of degree zero exist, all residue fields are finite over $\mathbf{Q}$, and the module of Kähler differentials is free of rank one), every place of either field has generating coordinate differential, $\Omega[\cdot \,\!/\mathbf{Q}]$ is nontrivial for both, both have a canonical divisor, and both satisfy the residue theorem (the Weil functional attached to a nonzero differential kills the diagonal adeles); moreover $\mathbf{Q}(M'.C)$ has principal divisors, both $\varphi'_\alpha$ and $\varphi'_\beta$ are integral ring maps and separable, traces along $\varphi'_\alpha$ carry elements integral at all places above $v$ to elements integral at $v$, and both maps satisfy the fibre residue identity: for every place $v$ of $\mathbf{Q}(X_{\mathbf{Q}})$, every $\omega \in \Omega[\mathbf{Q}(X_{\mathbf{Q}})/\mathbf{Q}]$ and every $f'$, the sum of the residue terms of $\varphi'^{*}\omega$ against the constant adele $f'$ over the places $w$ in the fibre of $v$ equals the residue term of $\omega$ against the constant adele $\operatorname{tr}(f')$ at $v$.
--
--   This is the function-field residue package for the two legs of the degeneracy roof computing the Hecke correspondence $T_q$ on the generic fibre: it assembles, once and for all over $\mathbf{Q}$, the facts about one-variable function fields (curve axioms, canonical divisor, residue theorem, separability and trace integrality, and the residue transfer formula along a finite map) that are needed downstream. It is used in identifying the Kähler-differential pullbacks of the two legs with the Hecke correspondence.
-- source:
